    {
      "id": "aud-m2-tbs1-ex1",
      "title": "Planning observations",
      "html": "<p>Complex warranty estimates require substantial judgment. The new ERP has not implemented approval controls. A lender covenant increases pressure to overstate earnings. The team initially planned interim testing before the ERP conversion.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "aud-m2-tbs1-ex2",
      "title": "Illustrative risk inputs",
      "html": "<p>For one assertion, acceptable audit risk is 3%, inherent risk is 60%, and control risk is 50%. These percentages are a teaching illustration, not a prescribed audit formula for every engagement.</p>"
    }
